  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nirvana-Jie/dsh-lark-agent/main/assets/plugin-icon.png\" width=\"80\" align=\"right\" alt=\"dsh-lark-agent icon\">"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-lark-agent",
      "text": "[中文](https://github.com/Nirvana-Jie/dsh-lark-agent/blob/main/README_zh.md)\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-lark-agent)\n\n**Reach your [DeepSeek Harness](https://www.deepseek.com/harness/) assistant from Feishu / Lark when you're away from your computer.**"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-lark-agent",
      "text": "dsh-lark-agent adds a Feishu / Lark private chat to a running DeepSeek Harness: hand off tasks, talk through plans, and pick up earlier topics from your phone. Feishu gets its own sessions and never takes over chats already open in the desktop app or on the web.\n\n[](https://github.com/Nirvana-Jie/dsh-lark-agent/blob/main/assets/readme/intro.mp4)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install / Update",
      "text": "Before you start:\n\n- DeepSeek Harness is running, can chat, and has a default model selected: PC App `0.2.1-rc.5` (`0.2.1-rc.2` and `rc.3` also work), or Web / `dsh` CLI `0.1.1-rc.2`.\n- The official Lark CLI is installed on the same machine **before** you enable the plugin (needs Node.js / npm):\n\n```sh\n  npm install -g @larksuite/cli@1.0.98\n  lark-cli --version\n  ```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install / Update",
      "text": "Don't run `lark-cli config init` or `lark-cli auth login`: the plugin creates its own dedicated CLI profile when you scan, and `config init` can overwrite existing profiles."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install on the DeepSeek Harness desktop app",
      "text": "In the sidebar, open **插件 → 添加插件** (Plugins → Add plugin), enter `dsh-lark-agent`, click **安装** (Install), then **立即启用** (Enable now). Restart if the app asks."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install with the `dsh` CLI",
      "text": "[`dsh plugin`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@deepseek-ai/dsh) runs pnpm, so pnpm must be on your PATH:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-lark-agent@0.6.2 --allow-build=protobufjs\n```\n\nThen restart `dsh web`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install with the `dsh` CLI",
      "text": "> [!NOTE]\n> `--allow-build=protobufjs` lets a dependency of the Lark SDK run its install script. Without it, pnpm 11 stops with `ERR_PNPM_IGNORED_BUILDS` and dsh does not enable the plugin. If that already happened, run:\n>\n> ```sh\n> dsh plugin --profile web approve-builds '!protobufjs'\n> ```\n>\n> The `!` skips that optional script (it only prints a version hint) and lets dsh finish enabling the plugin. Then restart `dsh web`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Update",
